// PIN (nested-match) — `match` nested under another construct trips the
// shape checker's nested-invocation path. validateFlow (top level) skips
// `@pass_ran`-stamped flows ("transform output is valid by construction",
// shape_checker.zig:477) but the nested pipeline-invocation check
// (shape_checker.zig:978-986) has NO such skip: it looks the transformed
// invocation up in the runtime events registry and raises UnknownEvent —
// silently (debug-log only). Same failure under ~for, ~if, or a plain
// runtime event's branch: the gap is "nested anywhere".
//
// This is the top-level vs in-flow duality surviving in the shape checker —
// the transform runner's fork was healed (site cursors, stage 3); this is
// the checker-side twin. Goes GREEN when nested validation mirrors the
// @pass_ran skip.
//
// The shape matters: it is the regex benchmark's hot loop
// (benchmarks/workloads/regex_match/koru/input.kz).
~import std/regex
~import std/io

~for(0..3)
! each _ |> match("foo@bar")
            | `[a-z]+@[a-z]+` _ |> std/io:print.ln("hit")
            | no-match _ |> std/io:print.ln("miss")
